00:13:01.850 --> 00:13:03.740
For the rest of
this discussion, we

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:06.620
are going to be focusing on
Android apps for Chromebooks.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:08.547
So, we are going to
talk about a few things.

00:13:08.547 --> 00:13:10.880
First, we are going to talk
about our design approaches,

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:12.500
and what kind of
design choices did we

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:16.130
make so that it would be a
consistent and good experience,

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:18.440
which adds to the
strength of the products,

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:21.635
so users get the best
possible experience.

00:13:21.635 --> 00:13:23.750
So, we'll talk about
some of the devices which

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:26.045
have been built recently,
which are optimized,

00:13:26.045 --> 00:13:28.340
or which are designed with
the Play Store in mind--

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:30.140
with the Google
Play Store in mind.

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:33.230
And then we are going to be
showing some app examples.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:36.650
We are going to be doing a
demo, show you some sample apps.

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:38.330
And then we are going
to end with tips

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:41.584
for optimizing your Android
apps on Chromebooks.

00:13:41.584 --> 00:13:44.000
So, that's a run through of
what we will be talking about.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:49.330
So, lets talk a little bit
about the design choices

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:50.910
which we made.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:55.950
So, Chrome OS is Google's
productivity operating system.

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:58.320
Because it's a productivity
operating system,

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:00.780
users want to be
able to multitask.

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:02.790
They want to be able to
use multiple windows.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.190
They want to be able to
resize their windows.

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:07.890
One of the things which
I think users really

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:10.020
love about Chromebooks,
is it comes

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:12.030
with a Chrome Browser,
the desktop Chrome

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:16.200
Browser, with support for full
extensions, tabs, productivity.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.540
So, the Chrome Browser is
there so you can still use

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.360
all of your web applications.

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:22.680
But the way we have brought
the Android applications

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:25.590
to Chromebooks is you
still get multiple windows

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.100
with your Android applications.

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:29.391
So, you could be running
different Android applications

00:14:29.391 --> 00:14:30.670
in different windows.

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:33.060
You can resize the
Android application

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:36.510
depending on the capability
of the application.

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:40.297
So, the design itself
is focused on ensuring

00:14:40.297 --> 00:14:41.880
that users can be
productive, and they

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:46.240
can do multitasking on
these large screens.

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:49.020
If manageability-- I think we
have already touched on that.

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:51.180
We made sure that
manageability was included.

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:56.320
It's a very-- so the simplicity
continues for administrators.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:57.430
Then, if you look at the--

00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:59.680
if you think about
Google Play, and if you

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:01.270
think about the
billions of users

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:04.030
who are using Android
applications in Android phones

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:05.980
today, we also
wanted to make sure

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:08.530
that they had a consistent
experience when they

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:10.540
started using these Android--

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:13.060
when they started using
the Android applications

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:15.240
on their Chrome devices.

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:19.010
So, Android applications
are touch optimized.

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:20.880
But Chromebooks have
different capabilities.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:22.770
In addition to-- some of
them have touchscreen,

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:23.560
some of them don't.

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.893
But they have capabilities--
like you have the trackpad.

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:30.620
So, just as you would
use your finger--

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:33.690
I have a precision
touch trackpad.

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:35.730
So, you can use your
trackpad in order

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:39.720
to navigate the touch elements
on these applications.

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:40.860
And you can click on them.

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:43.260
So, for a user who's used
to doing that on his phone--

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:45.360
when they come over here, it's
a very natural motion for them

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:46.651
to start using their track pad.

00:15:49.585 --> 00:15:51.585
Of course, they get their
familiar applications.

00:15:51.585 --> 00:15:54.880
The other thing, is if you look
at the Android applications,

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:59.200
most Android applications are
designed with offline in mind.

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:03.605
So, when I'm on an airplane and
I'm using my Android phone--

00:16:03.605 --> 00:16:05.980
I mean, obviously, I use the
Google Nexus or Google Pixel

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:07.150
phones.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.770
So, at that point I can do any--

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:10.210
I can work.

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:11.060
I can do a lot.

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:12.070
I can read books.

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.720
I can play games.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:16.330
I can listen to music.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.590
I can do a variety of things.

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:20.522
And it all works when
I'm disconnected,

00:16:20.522 --> 00:16:21.730
and when I'm on the airplane.

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:24.610
And I can do all of that
on my Android application

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:26.180
with my Chromebook as well.

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:27.960
So that's very good
for Chromebooks.

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:30.040
But that's also really
consistent from a user

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:31.605
point of view.

00:16:31.605 --> 00:16:33.430
The other thing is the
way we have brought

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.425
the Android applications,
or the Google Play

00:16:35.425 --> 00:16:39.070
Store to Chromebook, is that
it is a native implementation,

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:42.700
and it supports a wide
set of Android APIs.

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:44.350
So, from a user
perspective you're

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:46.360
going to get good performance.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:50.380
And you're going to get a
consistent UI experience.

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:53.230
So, again, we tried to just
go after the design in a way

00:16:53.230 --> 00:16:55.690
that it's a great
experience for people

00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:59.080
who are used to being productive
on their Chrome devices.

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.840
But also for the
users who are used

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:04.180
to using Android applications
on the Google Play Store,

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:06.970
they also get a very
positive and a really

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:08.777
good and consistent experience.

00:17:12.624 --> 00:17:15.380
So, in terms of what kind of
applications are available,

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:17.569
almost all Android
applications are

00:17:17.569 --> 00:17:19.670
eligible for Chrome devices.

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:21.920
Some exceptions are
going to be applications

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:23.960
which require special sensors.

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:26.569
So, if your application
requires a GPS,

00:17:26.569 --> 00:17:30.240
and a Chromebook does not have
GPS, we'll filter that out.

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:32.740
In terms of how users
are going to access--

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:34.620
so the applications--
so, remember

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:36.720
I said Chromebooks
are very shareable.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.090
Which means any user can
sign into any Chrome device

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:41.200
and they get that same
consistent experience.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.320
So, the Android
applications are also

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:47.100
tied to a user account, which
means that any Chromebook--

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:49.230
if I go from this Chromebook
to this Chromebook,

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:51.240
it will download my
Android applications,

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:53.732
and I'll be able to use them.

00:17:53.732 --> 00:17:55.940
And for those who have
purchased Android applications

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:58.160
on another device, the
same purchased application

00:17:58.160 --> 00:17:59.826
is going to work on
your Chrome devices.

00:18:04.335 --> 00:18:08.100
A little bit more details
about the app management part,

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:10.810
and how the Chrome device
management experiences.

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:16.850
It's centralized
application management.

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:19.190
So, as an administrator,
you're going

00:18:19.190 --> 00:18:22.070
to approve all Android
applications that

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:25.370
can be used in your managed
environment, for your managed

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:26.210
Chromebooks.

00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:27.800
So, it's a central opt-in model.

00:18:27.800 --> 00:18:29.390
You approve all of them.

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:32.300
And then, in terms of curating
the applications for the users,

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:34.440
it can be done in
two different ways.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:36.740
You can say that
your users can--

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:39.530
you allow your users to
install applications, which

00:18:39.530 --> 00:18:41.330
means it's your user's choice.

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:43.910
If they want, they can
install that application.

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:47.330
Or, you can push the
applications to the users

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:50.730
so it's default on their device
when they open up the device,

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.970
and when they log in.

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:56.610
Again, as an administrator
you have full control,

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.830
and you should be able to
manage all of your Android

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:01.797
applications in a way
that is very consistent,

00:19:01.797 --> 00:19:02.755
and it's also flexible.

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:08.460
And the unit is at
the OU level, which

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.397
means however you have
set up your user groups

00:19:10.397 --> 00:19:12.480
is going to work in terms
of managing your Android

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:13.256
application.

00:19:13.256 --> 00:19:15.630
So, if you're a business, if
you have multiple locations,

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:18.990
different functions, you want
to set up Android applications

00:19:18.990 --> 00:19:21.250
in different ways for
these user groups,

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:23.070
then you can do that
using the Chrome

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:24.500
administrative capabilities.

00:19:31.335 --> 00:19:33.630
So, one of my colleagues
gave a talk yesterday,

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:35.340
and as part of
that she announced

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:38.830
that Android Kiosks apps are
also coming to Chrome OS.

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:40.980
It'll come with the Chrome
OS 57 release, which

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:42.510
is literally in a few days.

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:45.270
Which means that on
your kiosk, if you're

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:47.151
using Chrome as a
kiosk device, which

00:19:47.151 --> 00:19:48.900
means you are running
a single application

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:50.880
in an immersive
mode, you will be

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:53.520
able to also run
Android apps there.

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:56.040
And some of the examples
of Android apps--

00:19:56.040 --> 00:20:00.630
one of the examples is, I think
Hyatt has a room control app.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:04.189
That's a kiosk app which
can run on your device.

00:20:04.189 --> 00:20:05.730
So, you could set
up a Chrome device,

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:08.100
if you have an equivalent
app in your hotel room,

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:10.590
and you could just use the
same Android application.

00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:12.090
Another one which
is being mentioned

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:14.173
is this crowdDJ, which is
for managing nightclubs,

00:20:14.173 --> 00:20:15.870
for those who are
in that business.

00:20:18.695 --> 00:20:22.110
So again, we wanted to make sure
that Android apps are supported

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:25.210
for all form factors
and all use cases.

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:28.410
So, we have that for the
general user use case,

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:29.820
but also for the
kiosk use cases.

00:20:34.139 --> 00:20:35.930
So, I'm going to switch
gears a little bit,

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:38.450
and I'm going to talk
to you about Android--

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:41.750
about the new Chromebooks, which
have been designed with Google

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:43.280
Play in mind.

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:45.920
So, as I said
before, we continue

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:47.366
to work with the OEM partners.

00:20:47.366 --> 00:20:48.740
And we pretty much
work with them

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:51.980
continuously to evolve
the range of Chromebooks.

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:55.370
And as part of the Google Play
Store coming to Chromebooks,

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:58.380
we wanted to make sure that
we had the right devices.

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:01.850
We were working on devices which
can really delight the users,

00:21:01.850 --> 00:21:04.321
in terms of the Android
application experience.

00:21:06.905 --> 00:21:11.810
So, at CES this year,
along with Samsung,

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:15.780
we announced Samsung Chromebook
Pro, and Sampson Chromebook

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:17.180
Plus.

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:20.120
So, these are devices, and
I have one of these here--

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:22.360
and we do have, by the
way, a few other devices,

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:25.010
if you have time later
to take a look at it.

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:27.180
So this is the Samsung
Chromebook Plus.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:31.820
So, its a convertible, so
you can use it as a notebook.

00:21:31.820 --> 00:21:33.980
The screen-- and you can
come check it out later.

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:36.320
Its a beautiful quad HD screen.

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:37.910
This actually has
a built in pen.

00:21:37.910 --> 00:21:40.510
So, it has a built in pen,
which you can take out.

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:43.170
So, now you're able to write
on these devices as well.

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:46.010
The other design choice
which we made, is it's

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:48.050
actually a 3 is to 2 screen.

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:50.590
What this means is that
the screen is squarer,

00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:53.900
but that means you can use it
as a tablet in any orientation.

00:21:57.050 --> 00:21:58.676
So, those are some
of the optimizations

00:21:58.676 --> 00:21:59.550
done on the hardware.

00:21:59.550 --> 00:22:00.860
And it's pretty thin and light.

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:03.110
So, you can come
and check it out.

00:22:03.110 --> 00:22:06.630
This comes with the Google Play
Store right out of the box.

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:08.880
Which means that you get
Android applications,

00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:11.250
and you can do more
things with this device

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:14.229
as soon as you get it to your
house, or to your business.

00:22:14.229 --> 00:22:16.520
And of course, it has all of
the goodness of the Chrome

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:17.360
Operating System.

00:22:17.360 --> 00:22:21.500
So, it has the speed, security,
simplicity, shareability,

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:23.780
and then, now a lot more
offline capabilities

00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:25.190
with the Android applications.

00:22:31.605 --> 00:22:34.360
So, in terms of
Chromebook Pro and Plus,

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:36.822
which are the two devices
which were announced,

00:22:36.822 --> 00:22:38.530
Chromebook Plus was
the one I showed you.

00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:40.690
It's already in market.

00:22:40.690 --> 00:22:43.440
And Chromebook Plus,
it's powered by an ARM,

00:22:43.440 --> 00:22:45.360
OP1 processor.

00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:49.390
Chromebook Pro will be
coming to market in April.

00:22:49.390 --> 00:22:51.520
It's going to be a
black color device.

00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:52.930
It's very professional looking.

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:57.040
And then, also, it's going
to have the Intel Core M3

00:22:57.040 --> 00:22:58.140
processor.

00:22:58.140 --> 00:23:00.600
So, it will be in
market in April,

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:02.975
but Plus is in market right now.

00:23:09.025 --> 00:23:11.530
So I also wanted to point
out that we have been working

00:23:11.530 --> 00:23:14.680
with the OEM partners
to build rugged devices,

00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:16.420
mainly for education use.

00:23:16.420 --> 00:23:19.090
So Acer, ASUS, HP--

00:23:19.090 --> 00:23:23.740
all of them announced devices
recently for rugged devices

00:23:23.740 --> 00:23:27.990
which are convertibles, and
which have stylus support.

00:23:27.990 --> 00:23:30.490
These are Chrome devices-- and
again, I have some of these--

00:23:30.490 --> 00:23:32.792
I have a couple of them here.

00:23:32.792 --> 00:23:34.000
You can check them out later.

00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:36.640
This is the Acer device, and
you can see it's pretty rugged.

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:39.650
This is the HP device, and
this is also a ruggged device.

00:23:39.650 --> 00:23:42.310
So, we expect schools to
start using these devices.

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:44.110
We are seeing a lot
of good interest.

00:23:44.110 --> 00:23:46.180
And then again, these
are convertible,

00:23:46.180 --> 00:23:47.845
and they come with pen.

00:23:47.845 --> 00:23:50.230
So, in terms of the pen
technology, we have--

00:23:50.230 --> 00:23:52.600
you can see the Samsung
devices have pen built in.

00:23:52.600 --> 00:23:54.454
These are a couple
of [? leg ?] pens.

00:23:54.454 --> 00:23:55.870
And again, if
you're a school, you

00:23:55.870 --> 00:23:58.350
can use different types of pens.

00:23:58.350 --> 00:24:00.010
The pen technology
which we are using

00:24:00.010 --> 00:24:04.062
is EMR, which means that the
pen itself is very affordable.

00:24:04.062 --> 00:24:05.020
It's not an active pen.

00:24:05.020 --> 00:24:07.330
You don't need to charge
it, which we think

00:24:07.330 --> 00:24:09.280
should be really positive.

00:24:09.280 --> 00:24:11.465
And while this is mainly
designed for education,

00:24:11.465 --> 00:24:13.840
we are hitting some interesting
use cases from businesses

00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:14.725
as well.

00:24:14.725 --> 00:24:16.600
So, one of the use cases
which we are hearing

00:24:16.600 --> 00:24:21.400
is for backroom
software, like retailers,

00:24:21.400 --> 00:24:24.100
for people who want to do
their inventory management.

00:24:24.100 --> 00:24:25.930
They are interested
in devices like this,

00:24:25.930 --> 00:24:28.480
because they also have one
interesting new feature, which

00:24:28.480 --> 00:24:30.070
we didn't have on
Chromebooks before.

00:24:30.070 --> 00:24:32.590
They actually have
a second camera,

00:24:32.590 --> 00:24:34.070
which is on the c panel.

00:24:34.070 --> 00:24:36.910
Which means that you
could use these devices--

00:24:36.910 --> 00:24:39.700
I could just go over them, and
there's a camera over here,

00:24:39.700 --> 00:24:41.290
so I could take
photos of storerooms,

00:24:41.290 --> 00:24:44.840
and I could record that.

00:24:44.840 --> 00:24:47.164
So, we are starting to
diversify the range of devices.

00:24:47.164 --> 00:24:48.580
Obviously, these
are the first set

00:24:48.580 --> 00:24:49.889
of devices which have come in.

00:24:49.889 --> 00:24:51.430
Again, depending on
your application,

00:24:51.430 --> 00:24:53.170
we are trying to go
more into, you know,

00:24:53.170 --> 00:24:54.340
you can use it as a tablet.

00:24:54.340 --> 00:24:55.450
You can use it as a PC.

00:24:55.450 --> 00:24:57.370
You can have different
forms of input.

00:24:57.370 --> 00:24:58.450
You can touch.

00:24:58.450 --> 00:24:59.680
You can write.

00:24:59.680 --> 00:25:01.600
You can obviously type on it.

00:25:04.240 --> 00:25:07.780
And they will continue
to evolve in the future.

00:25:07.780 --> 00:25:12.746
So with that, I'm going to
